                                                "sense_id": "52d95c42-068e-3929-a95f-49f9eabd0f3e",
                                                "text": "Pidgin is a combination of expressions and phrases that are recognizable to those who speak it. To non-Pidgin speakers, it may sound like slang. For example, “dat” means that and “fadda” means father or dad."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4ed6fdad-ca3b-4060-ac5c-44b0c944e2c6",
                                                "sense_id": "52d95c42-068e-3929-a95f-49f9eabd0f3e",
                                                "text": "This variation is strikingly similar to the Work’s so-called “ballooned droplet” within the circle. The figure in the Work is slightly more bulbous, but it is instantly recognizable as a quotation mark."
